Chromium 87 ships this generator as Python 2 and the build runs it as
"python", which on this machine is 3.14. Three constructs are syntax errors
there, and the first one aborts at parse time -- before any argument is read --
so the target fails with SyntaxError rather than anything about file types:

    print "ERROR: ..."        ->  print("ERROR: ...")   (x2)
    PlatformTypes().iteritems()  ->  PlatformTypes().items()

The alternative was pointing this one script at a Python 2, which Haiku does
not package, or at the vendored one in third_party, which Chromium 87 does not
carry for the host. Converting three lines is smaller than either and matches
what upstream did to this same file in later branches.

Note the -t linux argument in the failing command line: this generator has no
Haiku platform type and is told to produce the Linux tables. That is
deliberate and unrelated -- download file-type policy is not
platform-specific in any way that matters to a browser shell.

--- a/chromium/components/safe_browsing/core/resources/gen_file_type_proto.py
+++ b/chromium/components/safe_browsing/core/resources/gen_file_type_proto.py
@@ -154,7 +154,7 @@
       FilterForPlatformAndWrite(pb, platform_enum, outfile)
     else:
       # Make a separate file for each platform
-      for platform_type, platform_enum in PlatformTypes().iteritems():
+      for platform_type, platform_enum in PlatformTypes().items():
         # e.g. .../all/77/chromeos/download_file_types.pb
         outfile = os.path.join(opts.outdir,
                                str(pb.version_id),
@@ -179,12 +179,12 @@
 
   def VerifyArgs(self, opts):
     if (not opts.all and opts.type not in PlatformTypes()):
-      print "ERROR: Unknown platform type '%s'" % opts.type
+      print("ERROR: Unknown platform type '%s'" % opts.type)
       self.opt_parser.print_help()
       return False
 
     if (bool(opts.all) == bool(opts.type)):
-      print "ERROR: Need exactly one of --type or --all"
+      print("ERROR: Need exactly one of --type or --all")
